                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><span style="font-family: 'times new roman', times, serif;">This course consists of both theoretical and experimental sections. The theoretical section comprises 21 credit hours, covering the fundamental concepts of forensic toxicology, influencing factors of poisoning incidents, and forensic identification of poisoning, as well as the toxicological mechanisms and key points of forensic identification for various common types of poisoning. The experimental section includes 12 credit hours, with a total of 3 experiments: barbiturates, carbon monoxide, and organophosphorus pesticides. The experimental content encompasses both the observation of poisoning symptoms caused by toxic substances and the detection and analysis of these substances.</span></p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
